Veteran journalist Miranda Spivack, who spent 20 years as an award-winning editor and reporter for the Washington Post, will speak about her book Backroom Deals in Our Backyards at 7 p.m. on July 8. She will be interviewed by Michael Morisy, Founder & Chief Executive of MuckRock.

Backroom Deals in Our Backyards tells the story of five accidental activists from across the United States who started questioning why their local and state governments didn’t protect them from issues facing their communities and why there was a frightening lack of transparency surrounding the way these issues were resolved. The secret deals, lies, and corruption they uncover shake their faith in government but move them to action.

@headhousebooks will be there selling this awesome book!

World Cafe Live x SORI present 
K-Folk Rock Fest in Philly! 🎸🥁🇰🇷🔥

Feel the raw energy of Korean Folk Rock as Sangjaru and Insun Park & Generals take the stage direct from South Korea. This high voltage double bill brings two fearless bands together, where deep rooted tradition collides with loud guitars, driving rhythms, and rock spirit.

@koreangipsy_sangjaru Sangjaru tears into Korean traditional music with gypsy swing, funk, rock, and improvisation, delivering a sound that is bold, playful, and constantly in motion. @c.sungyoon @seoooonghun @jang_gu_boy 

@insun.janggoon Insun Park & Generals unleash a powerful fusion of rock, Korean traditional music, and mask dance beats. Led by Insun Park, a master of the Gangnyeong Mask Dance and National Intangible Cultural Heritage holder, the group combines pounding rhythms, commanding vocals, and high energy movement. @parkin_sun @hyoungki506 @johyun_zzz @darkgomtang @donghyukkkkk 

